The structure specifies a time value in seconds and microseconds.
The values in are opaque types whose length may vary on different
machines;  depending on them to have any given length may lead to
errors.  The structure indicates the local time zone (measured in
minutes of time westward from Greenwich), and  a  flag  that,  if
nonzero, indicates that Daylight Saving time applies locally dur‐
ing  the  appropriate  part of the year.  Only the super‐user may
set the time of day or time zone.  If the system  securelevel  is
greater  than 1 (see the time may only be advanced.  This limita‐
tion is imposed to prevent a malicious  super‐user  from  setting
arbitrary time stamps on files.  The system time can still be ad‐
justed  backwards  using  the system call even when the system is
secure.  A 0 return value indicates that the call  succeeded.   A
